# Blog Migrator - Troubleshooting & Common Issues

## Common Errors

### "Failed to parse URL from..."
**Cause**: URL has extra characters (quotes, whitespace).

**Common scenario**: Extracting featured image from CSS `background-image`.

**Fix**: Use regex to strip all URL wrapper characters:
```js
getValue: (el) => el.style.backgroundImage.replace(/url\(['"]?/, '').replace(/['"]?\)/, '')
```

### "filter is not a function"
**Cause**: `filter` property in config is not a function.

**Fix**: Ensure filter is a function:
```js
filter: (url) => true,                    // ✓ Correct
filter: true,                             // ✗ Wrong
```

### "Cannot read properties of null (reading 'dataset')"
**Cause**: Selector returned null, but `getValue` tried to access properties.

**Fix**: Check element exists before accessing, or use optional chaining:
```js
getValue: (el) => el?.dataset?.src || el?.src || ''
```

### "window is not defined"
**Cause**: Trying to use browser globals in Node.js (usually in config functions).

**Fix**: Only use element properties passed to getValue, not global objects:
```js
getValue: (el) => window.getComputedStyle(el)  // ✗ Wrong
getValue: (el) => el.style.backgroundImage     // ✓ Correct
```

### Featured image not downloading
**Cause**: Featured image selector returns URL in unexpected format.

**Debug**: Log the extracted URL:
```js
getValue: (el) => {
    const url = el.style.backgroundImage;
    console.log('Raw URL:', url);
    return url.replace(/url\(['"]?/, '').replace(/['"]?\)/, '');
}
```

### Broken image syntax in markdown output (linked images)
**Cause**: Images wrapped in `<a>` tags were converted by Turndown to linked image syntax with broken newlines.

**Solution**: Fixed in v8 with custom `linkedImages` Turndown rule. This is handled automatically - no config needed.

### Some images still have remote URLs
**Cause**: Download failed for those specific images (network error, 404, etc).

**Symptom**: Summary shows "Pages with remote images" and markdown files contain `![](https://...)` URLs.

**Solution**: Check the console warnings for specific failures. Common causes:
- Image URL returned 404
- Network timeout
- URL blocked by server

You can use the `filter` function to skip problematic URLs:
```js
filter: (url) => {
    // Skip external CDN that blocks requests
    if (url.includes('getnarrativeapp.com')) return false;
    return true;
}
```

## Debugging Tips

### Check what's being extracted
Add console.log in config functions:
```js
getValue: (el) => {
    const value = el.textContent;
    console.log('Extracted:', value);
    return value.trim();
}
```

### Test selectors in browser
```js
// In browser console on target page:
document.querySelector('.background-inner')?.style.backgroundImage
document.querySelector('.heading-text h1')?.textContent
```

## Site-Specific Issues

### Uncode WordPress Theme (Philip Quinnell Photography)
- Featured image: Background image on `.background-inner`
- Post body: `.post-body`
- Title: `.heading-text h1`

### Third-party embeds (Narrative, etc)
Some posts embed content from third-party services like Narrative. These images may fail to download if the CDN blocks automated requests.

**Solution**: Use the filter function to skip these:
```js
filter: (url) => !url.includes('getnarrativeapp.com')
```

## Performance Notes

- Tool processes URLs sequentially (not parallel)
- Large images may take time to download
- Consider adding delay between requests if hitting rate limits

## Validation

### Check output markdown
```yaml
---
title: Example Title
image: /assets/uploads/slug-featured.jpg
imageAlt: Alt text here
---

Content with images:
![alt text](/assets/uploads/slug-01.jpg)
```

### Verify images downloaded
```bash
ls downloads/images/
```

### Check for null fields in summary
The summary report shows which pages have missing data - update selectors or accept nulls.
